    'pet-name-meaning-lookup', 'Pet Name Meaning Lookup', 'Search 25+ of the most popular dog and cat names to see their linguistic origin, literal meaning, and personality vibe. Helpful when you''re deciding between shortlisted names or want a story to tell friends about the name you picked.',
    'Pet Name Meaning Lookup — Free Pet Tool',
    'Search 25+ of the most popular dog and cat names to see their linguistic origin, literal meaning, and personality vibe. Helpful when you''re deciding between shortlisted names or want a story to tell friends about the name you picked.', 0, 0, 169
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'adoption-vs-buying-cost-comparator', 'Adoption vs Buying Cost Comparator', 'Compare the true first-year cost of adopting a pet from a shelter versus buying from a breeder or pet store. Adoption fees typically include spay/neuter, core vaccines, and microchipping — services that add $500-$800 when you buy a pet elsewhere. Enter local prices to get a personalized side-by-side breakdown of both paths and see the real dollar difference before you bring a pet home.',
    'Adoption vs Buying Cost Comparator — Free Pet Tool',
    'Compare the true first-year cost of adopting a pet from a shelter versus buying from a breeder or pet store. Adoption fees typically include spay/neuter, core vaccines, and microchipping — services that add $500-$800 when you buy a pet elsewhere. Enter local prices to get a personalized side-by-side breakdown of both paths and see the real dollar difference before you bring a pet home.', 0, 0, 170
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'litter-size-predictor', 'Litter Size Predictor', 'Predict how many puppies, kittens, or rabbit kits to expect in a litter based on breed size category, the mother''s age, and how many times she has bred before. Litter size varies widely — a Chihuahua averages 3 puppies while a Great Dane may deliver 12 — and first-time mothers typically produce fewer offspring than experienced dams in their prime. Use this as an educational planning estimate before your reproductive veterinarian confirms the count with ultrasound or X-ray.',
    'Litter Size Predictor — Free Pet Tool',
    'Predict how many puppies, kittens, or rabbit kits to expect in a litter based on breed size category, the mother''s age, and how many times she has bred before. Litter size varies widely — a Chihuahua averages 3 puppies while a Great Dane may deliver 12 — and first-time mothers typically produce fewer offspring than experienced dams in their prime. Use this as an educational planning estimate before your reproductive veterinarian confirms the count with ultrasound or X-ray.', 0, 0, 171
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'clicker-training-planner', 'Clicker Training Planner', 'Clicker training is the gold standard of modern, force-free animal learning. The click sound becomes a precise marker your pet learns to trust — it says ''that exact behavior earned you a treat.'' This planner walks you through the six-phase timeline used by professional trainers: charging the clicker, capturing behaviors, luring, adding cue words, proofing under distraction, and finally thinning food rewards. It works for dogs, cats, parrots, rabbits, ferrets, and even horses, and it produces cleaner learning than voice-only markers because it eliminates tone variation and body-language noise.',
    'Clicker Training Planner — Free Pet Tool',
    'Clicker training is the gold standard of modern, force-free animal learning. The click sound becomes a precise marker your pet learns to trust — it says ''that exact behavior earned you a treat.'' This planner walks you through the six-phase timeline used by professional trainers: charging the clicker, capturing behaviors, luring, adding cue words, proofing under distraction, and finally thinning food rewards. It works for dogs, cats, parrots, rabbits, ferrets, and even horses, and it produces cleaner learning than voice-only markers because it eliminates tone variation and body-language noise.', 0, 0, 172
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'potty-training-schedule', 'Potty Training Schedule', 'House training is the number-one reason puppies get returned to shelters — and it''s almost always fixable with better scheduling. Puppies can hold their bladder for roughly their age-in-months in hours (a 3-month-old holds ~3 hours), and they need to go out after every meal, nap, play session, and training block. This tool builds a personalized daily schedule from your puppy''s age and your household''s wake/bedtime hours, so you can post it on the fridge and stop guessing.',
    'Potty Training Schedule — Free Pet Tool',
    'House training is the number-one reason puppies get returned to shelters — and it''s almost always fixable with better scheduling. Puppies can hold their bladder for roughly their age-in-months in hours (a 3-month-old holds ~3 hours), and they need to go out after every meal, nap, play session, and training block. This tool builds a personalized daily schedule from your puppy''s age and your household''s wake/bedtime hours, so you can post it on the fridge and stop guessing.', 0, 0, 173
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'crate-training-timeline', 'Crate Training Timeline', 'Done well, the crate is one of the most valuable tools in modern dog training — it accelerates house training, keeps puppies safe when unsupervised, and gives adult dogs a portable den for travel and vet stays. Done poorly, it creates lifelong panic and barrier frustration. This timeline follows the standard veterinary behavior progression: three weeks of gradual desensitization from ''crate is a magical treat dispenser'' to ''sleeps peacefully overnight and during your workday.'' Rushing this timeline is the single biggest cause of crate hate.',
    'Crate Training Timeline — Free Pet Tool',
    'Done well, the crate is one of the most valuable tools in modern dog training — it accelerates house training, keeps puppies safe when unsupervised, and gives adult dogs a portable den for travel and vet stays. Done poorly, it creates lifelong panic and barrier frustration. This timeline follows the standard veterinary behavior progression: three weeks of gradual desensitization from ''crate is a magical treat dispenser'' to ''sleeps peacefully overnight and during your workday.'' Rushing this timeline is the single biggest cause of crate hate.', 0, 0, 174
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'leash-training-progress', 'Leash Training Progress', 'A dog that pulls on leash isn''t ''stubborn'' — they''re simply on a schedule of continuous reinforcement, because every step of pulling gets them where they want to go. Loose-leash walking is a trained skill built one criterion at a time: first indoors, then in the yard, then around distractions. This tracker lists the ten measurable milestones that certified trainers use, from ''wears the leash calmly indoors'' to ''passes another dog under threshold.'' Tick each one as you go and progress persists on your device.',
    'Leash Training Progress — Free Pet Tool',
    'A dog that pulls on leash isn''t ''stubborn'' — they''re simply on a schedule of continuous reinforcement, because every step of pulling gets them where they want to go. Loose-leash walking is a trained skill built one criterion at a time: first indoors, then in the yard, then around distractions. This tracker lists the ten measurable milestones that certified trainers use, from ''wears the leash calmly indoors'' to ''passes another dog under threshold.'' Tick each one as you go and progress persists on your device.', 0, 0, 175
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'recall-training-tracker', 'Recall Training Tracker', 'Recall — coming when called — is the most important behavior any pet will learn, and the hardest to build reliably. This tracker lets you log every recall attempt across environments, from indoors to busy parks, so you can watch your reliability percentage grow over time. Certified trainers use the ''90% rule'': you should not trust your dog off-leash in unfenced areas until they hit 90%+ reliability across at least 20 sessions in that environment. Guessing your dog''s reliability without data is why so many pets are lost each year.',
    'Recall Training Tracker — Free Pet Tool',
    'Recall — coming when called — is the most important behavior any pet will learn, and the hardest to build reliably. This tracker lets you log every recall attempt across environments, from indoors to busy parks, so you can watch your reliability percentage grow over time. Certified trainers use the ''90% rule'': you should not trust your dog off-leash in unfenced areas until they hit 90%+ reliability across at least 20 sessions in that environment. Guessing your dog''s reliability without data is why so many pets are lost each year.', 0, 0, 176
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'socialization-checklist', 'Puppy Socialization Checklist', 'The socialization window closes between 12-16 weeks of age — after that, novelty exposure creates suspicion instead of confidence. A puppy who meets 100 friendly people, calmly experiences 50 environments, and hears 30 unusual sounds before 16 weeks grows into a stable adult dog. A puppy that only meets family and other dogs grows into a reactive, fearful adult that costs thousands in behavior consultants. This checklist covers the five categories AVSAB recommends: people, animals, environments, surfaces & sounds, and handling.',
    'Puppy Socialization Checklist — Free Pet Tool',
    'The socialization window closes between 12-16 weeks of age — after that, novelty exposure creates suspicion instead of confidence. A puppy who meets 100 friendly people, calmly experiences 50 environments, and hears 30 unusual sounds before 16 weeks grows into a stable adult dog. A puppy that only meets family and other dogs grows into a reactive, fearful adult that costs thousands in behavior consultants. This checklist covers the five categories AVSAB recommends: people, animals, environments, surfaces & sounds, and handling.', 0, 0, 177
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'puppy-milestone-tracker', 'Puppy Milestone Tracker', 'Puppy development follows a predictable timeline — eyes open at week 3, adult teeth erupt around week 16, and hormonal maturity arrives between 6-12 months depending on breed size. Missing a milestone by more than 1-2 weeks warrants a veterinary check-in. This tracker lists the ten most important developmental checkpoints, each with the typical week it occurs and what to watch for. Tick them off as they happen and keep this list handy for vet visits.',
    'Puppy Milestone Tracker — Free Pet Tool',
    'Puppy development follows a predictable timeline — eyes open at week 3, adult teeth erupt around week 16, and hormonal maturity arrives between 6-12 months depending on breed size. Missing a milestone by more than 1-2 weeks warrants a veterinary check-in. This tracker lists the ten most important developmental checkpoints, each with the typical week it occurs and what to watch for. Tick them off as they happen and keep this list handy for vet visits.', 0, 0, 178
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'aggression-risk-assessment', 'Aggression Risk Assessment', 'Aggression in pets is almost always fear-based and predictable — most bites are preceded by weeks or months of warning signs that owners miss or minimize. This screening tool walks through eight evidence-based risk factors used by certified veterinary behaviorists: resource guarding, freezing, hard stares, snapping, and bite history. It does not diagnose aggression, but it flags whether you should seek professional help. Any positive answer to a bite-history question warrants immediate consultation with a veterinary behaviorist (Dip ACVB).',
    'Aggression Risk Assessment — Free Pet Tool',
    'Aggression in pets is almost always fear-based and predictable — most bites are preceded by weeks or months of warning signs that owners miss or minimize. This screening tool walks through eight evidence-based risk factors used by certified veterinary behaviorists: resource guarding, freezing, hard stares, snapping, and bite history. It does not diagnose aggression, but it flags whether you should seek professional help. Any positive answer to a bite-history question warrants immediate consultation with a veterinary behaviorist (Dip ACVB).', 0, 0, 179
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'separation-anxiety-score', 'Separation Anxiety Score', 'Separation-related distress affects 20-40% of pet dogs and is one of the most misunderstood behavior problems. It is not ''being spoiled'' or ''acting out'' — it is a genuine panic disorder that resembles a human panic attack. Dogs experiencing it can urinate, destroy doors, or injure themselves within minutes of being left alone. This assessment scores eight validated indicators from the Overall/CSAT screening framework and provides a severity band: minimal, mild, moderate, or severe. Mild cases often respond to enrichment and slow absence training; moderate to severe cases benefit from medication and specialist support.',
    'Separation Anxiety Score — Free Pet Tool',
    'Separation-related distress affects 20-40% of pet dogs and is one of the most misunderstood behavior problems. It is not ''being spoiled'' or ''acting out'' — it is a genuine panic disorder that resembles a human panic attack. Dogs experiencing it can urinate, destroy doors, or injure themselves within minutes of being left alone. This assessment scores eight validated indicators from the Overall/CSAT screening framework and provides a severity band: minimal, mild, moderate, or severe. Mild cases often respond to enrichment and slow absence training; moderate to severe cases benefit from medication and specialist support.', 0, 0, 180
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'trick-training-library', 'Trick Training Library', 'Trick training is more than a party trick — it builds focus, exercises the brain, and strengthens the human-animal bond. Ten minutes of trick training tires most dogs more than an hour of walking. This library lists eleven classic tricks organized by difficulty, from ''Sit'' to ''Put toys away,'' each with the exact luring and shaping steps used by professional trainers. Filter by level to find your next challenge, and remember: every trick is trained in tiny increments, not one big leap.',
    'Trick Training Library — Free Pet Tool',
    'Trick training is more than a party trick — it builds focus, exercises the brain, and strengthens the human-animal bond. Ten minutes of trick training tires most dogs more than an hour of walking. This library lists eleven classic tricks organized by difficulty, from ''Sit'' to ''Put toys away,'' each with the exact luring and shaping steps used by professional trainers. Filter by level to find your next challenge, and remember: every trick is trained in tiny increments, not one big leap.', 0, 0, 181
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'command-vocabulary-builder', 'Command Vocabulary Builder', 'The average pet dog understands 165 words; exceptional dogs learn 1,000+ (Chaser the Border Collie learned 1,022 nouns in controlled studies). Every cue you teach is a fresh channel of communication that reduces frustration on both sides. This builder starts with five foundational commands (Sit, Down, Come, Stay, Leave it) and lets you add unlimited new cues with their meanings. Tick off which are mastered and see your total vocabulary grow — a wonderful record to bring to every vet or trainer visit.',
    'Command Vocabulary Builder — Free Pet Tool',
    'The average pet dog understands 165 words; exceptional dogs learn 1,000+ (Chaser the Border Collie learned 1,022 nouns in controlled studies). Every cue you teach is a fresh channel of communication that reduces frustration on both sides. This builder starts with five foundational commands (Sit, Down, Come, Stay, Leave it) and lets you add unlimited new cues with their meanings. Tick off which are mastered and see your total vocabulary grow — a wonderful record to bring to every vet or trainer visit.', 0, 0, 182
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'behavior-journal', 'Pet Behavior Journal', 'Most behavior ''mysteries'' aren''t mysteries — they''re patterns waiting to be seen. Journaling for two weeks reveals what actually triggers your pet''s barking, growling, or anxiety, versus what you assume triggers it. This journal captures the ABC of behavior science: Antecedent (what happened right before), Behavior (what your pet did), and Consequence (your response). Add a note field for context. Bring the last 30 entries to your veterinary behaviorist or trainer — the pattern often reveals the diagnosis before words do.',
    'Pet Behavior Journal — Free Pet Tool',
    'Most behavior ''mysteries'' aren''t mysteries — they''re patterns waiting to be seen. Journaling for two weeks reveals what actually triggers your pet''s barking, growling, or anxiety, versus what you assume triggers it. This journal captures the ABC of behavior science: Antecedent (what happened right before), Behavior (what your pet did), and Consequence (your response). Add a note field for context. Bring the last 30 entries to your veterinary behaviorist or trainer — the pattern often reveals the diagnosis before words do.', 0, 0, 183
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'reward-schedule-calculator', 'Reward Schedule Calculator', 'When to reward — and how often — is what separates trained dogs from dogs who only work if they see a treat. Continuous reinforcement (reward every rep) is essential during learning but destroys reliability if kept forever. Variable reinforcement (reward unpredictably) is what makes trained behaviors permanent — the same principle that makes slot machines addictive. This tool tells you exactly what reinforcement schedule to use for each training stage: acquisition, fluency, generalization, or maintenance.',
    'Reward Schedule Calculator — Free Pet Tool',
    'When to reward — and how often — is what separates trained dogs from dogs who only work if they see a treat. Continuous reinforcement (reward every rep) is essential during learning but destroys reliability if kept forever. Variable reinforcement (reward unpredictably) is what makes trained behaviors permanent — the same principle that makes slot machines addictive. This tool tells you exactly what reinforcement schedule to use for each training stage: acquisition, fluency, generalization, or maintenance.', 0, 0, 184
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'barking-log', 'Barking Log', 'Excessive barking is the number-one complaint neighbors report to animal control — and the number-one reason dogs are surrendered to shelters. But ''excessive barking'' is rarely one problem; it''s usually 3-4 different triggers running on the same pattern. This log lets you record every notable bark event with its trigger and duration, then automatically ranks your top triggers so you can address the biggest one first. Two weeks of logging usually reveals the culprit that''s driving 60-80% of the barking.',
    'Barking Log — Free Pet Tool',
    'Excessive barking is the number-one complaint neighbors report to animal control — and the number-one reason dogs are surrendered to shelters. But ''excessive barking'' is rarely one problem; it''s usually 3-4 different triggers running on the same pattern. This log lets you record every notable bark event with its trigger and duration, then automatically ranks your top triggers so you can address the biggest one first. Two weeks of logging usually reveals the culprit that''s driving 60-80% of the barking.', 0, 0, 185
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'litter-training-planner', 'Litter Training Planner (Cats & Rabbits)', 'Cats and rabbits are two of the easiest species to litter train — they instinctively prefer a consistent bathroom spot — but the setup is completely different for each. Cats need unscented clumping litter in a low-traffic box with the ''1 per cat + 1'' rule. Rabbits need paper-based litter, hay on top, and never clumping clay (which is toxic if ingested). This planner walks through the 3-week timeline for each species, from first setup to reliable free-roam privileges. Regression after training is usually medical (UTI, stones) — not behavioral.',
    'Litter Training Planner (Cats & Rabbits) — Free Pet Tool',
    'Cats and rabbits are two of the easiest species to litter train — they instinctively prefer a consistent bathroom spot — but the setup is completely different for each. Cats need unscented clumping litter in a low-traffic box with the ''1 per cat + 1'' rule. Rabbits need paper-based litter, hay on top, and never clumping clay (which is toxic if ingested). This planner walks through the 3-week timeline for each species, from first setup to reliable free-roam privileges. Regression after training is usually medical (UTI, stones) — not behavioral.', 0, 0, 186
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'heat-cycle-tracker', 'Heat Cycle Tracker (Dog, Cat, Rabbit)', 'Understanding your intact female''s heat cycle is essential whether you''re breeding intentionally or simply avoiding unwanted litters. This tracker records each observed stage — proestrus, estrus, diestrus, anestrus — and estimates the next expected cycle based on species-typical intervals: roughly every 6 months for dogs, every 2-3 weeks during breeding season for cats, and continuously receptive (induced ovulator) for rabbits. Consistent logging helps identify silent heats, split heats, prolonged bleeding, and pyometra risk factors long before they become emergencies.',
    'Heat Cycle Tracker (Dog, Cat, Rabbit) — Free Pet Tool',
    'Understanding your intact female''s heat cycle is essential whether you''re breeding intentionally or simply avoiding unwanted litters. This tracker records each observed stage — proestrus, estrus, diestrus, anestrus — and estimates the next expected cycle based on species-typical intervals: roughly every 6 months for dogs, every 2-3 weeks during breeding season for cats, and continuously receptive (induced ovulator) for rabbits. Consistent logging helps identify silent heats, split heats, prolonged bleeding, and pyometra risk factors long before they become emergencies.', 0, 0, 187
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'pregnancy-calendar', 'Pregnancy Calendar (Species-Specific)', 'Enter the mating date and pick your species — dog, cat, rabbit, guinea pig, hamster, ferret, horse, goat, or sheep — and get a personalized pregnancy calendar with due date, trimester markers, vet-check milestones, and nesting-prep deadlines. Dogs (63 days), cats (65 days), rabbits (31 days), horses (340 days) — each species has a distinct gestation length and a different rhythm of physical and behavioral changes. Knowing what to expect week by week is the difference between a smooth delivery and a preventable emergency.',
    'Pregnancy Calendar (Species-Specific) — Free Pet Tool',
    'Enter the mating date and pick your species — dog, cat, rabbit, guinea pig, hamster, ferret, horse, goat, or sheep — and get a personalized pregnancy calendar with due date, trimester markers, vet-check milestones, and nesting-prep deadlines. Dogs (63 days), cats (65 days), rabbits (31 days), horses (340 days) — each species has a distinct gestation length and a different rhythm of physical and behavioral changes. Knowing what to expect week by week is the difference between a smooth delivery and a preventable emergency.', 1, 0, 188
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'whelping-kittening-checklist', 'Whelping / Kittening Prep Checklist', 'The two weeks before a litter arrives are when most preventable problems are avoided. This checklist walks through every physical item you need in your whelping kit, how to set up a proper whelping or kittening box, what to discuss with your vet at the 55-day check, and the critical postpartum monitoring window (colostrum, weight, mom''s temperature). Skip any of these steps and a routine birth can turn into an emergency at 2 a.m.',
    'Whelping / Kittening Prep Checklist — Free Pet Tool',
    'The two weeks before a litter arrives are when most preventable problems are avoided. This checklist walks through every physical item you need in your whelping kit, how to set up a proper whelping or kittening box, what to discuss with your vet at the 55-day check, and the critical postpartum monitoring window (colostrum, weight, mom''s temperature). Skip any of these steps and a routine birth can turn into an emergency at 2 a.m.', 0, 0, 189
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'stud-fee-calculator', 'Stud Fee Calculator', 'Pricing a stud fee correctly is one of the harder decisions in ethical breeding. Undercharge and you devalue your stud''s line; overcharge and quality bitches go elsewhere. This calculator uses the industry-standard formula — average puppy price × stud quality multiplier — to suggest a fair cash fee, and compares it to a pick-of-litter arrangement. Pet-quality males typically fetch 40% of one puppy price, titled dogs 100%, champions 150%, and proven top producers with imported bloodlines 200%+.',
    'Stud Fee Calculator — Free Pet Tool',
    'Pricing a stud fee correctly is one of the harder decisions in ethical breeding. Undercharge and you devalue your stud''s line; overcharge and quality bitches go elsewhere. This calculator uses the industry-standard formula — average puppy price × stud quality multiplier — to suggest a fair cash fee, and compares it to a pick-of-litter arrangement. Pet-quality males typically fetch 40% of one puppy price, titled dogs 100%, champions 150%, and proven top producers with imported bloodlines 200%+.', 0, 0, 190
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'genetic-diversity-calculator', 'Genetic Diversity / COI Calculator', 'The Coefficient of Inbreeding (COI) is the single most important number in ethical breeding decisions. It measures how genetically similar the sire and dam are — the higher the number, the greater the risk that hidden recessive diseases will express in the litter. This calculator gives a quick estimate based on shared ancestors and generations back, plus context on what each COI band means (0-6.25% ideal, 25%+ full-sibling level and dangerous). For final decisions, always run a full 10-generation pedigree COI through breed-club or veterinary software.',
    'Genetic Diversity / COI Calculator — Free Pet Tool',
    'The Coefficient of Inbreeding (COI) is the single most important number in ethical breeding decisions. It measures how genetically similar the sire and dam are — the higher the number, the greater the risk that hidden recessive diseases will express in the litter. This calculator gives a quick estimate based on shared ancestors and generations back, plus context on what each COI band means (0-6.25% ideal, 25%+ full-sibling level and dangerous). For final decisions, always run a full 10-generation pedigree COI through breed-club or veterinary software.', 0, 0, 191
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'puppy-kitten-weight-chart', 'Puppy & Kitten Weight Chart', 'In the first four weeks of life, weight is the single most reliable indicator of a newborn''s health. Puppies and kittens should gain 5-10% of their body weight every day — a plateau of even 12 hours is a genuine emergency. This tracker logs every weigh-in (grams, not ounces — accuracy matters at this stage), plots gain since the previous session, and flags any stagnation. Reference ranges are conservative averages; small toy breeds and giant breeds will fall well outside typical numbers, so trend matters more than absolute weight.',
    'Puppy & Kitten Weight Chart — Free Pet Tool',
    'In the first four weeks of life, weight is the single most reliable indicator of a newborn''s health. Puppies and kittens should gain 5-10% of their body weight every day — a plateau of even 12 hours is a genuine emergency. This tracker logs every weigh-in (grams, not ounces — accuracy matters at this stage), plots gain since the previous session, and flags any stagnation. Reference ranges are conservative averages; small toy breeds and giant breeds will fall well outside typical numbers, so trend matters more than absolute weight.', 0, 0, 192
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'weaning-schedule', 'Weaning Schedule (Puppies, Kittens, Rabbits)', 'Weaning is a gradual process, not a switch. Puppies and kittens should be introduced to solid food around week 3-4, transitioned over 3-5 weeks, and fully weaned by week 7-8 — but they should stay with mom and littermates for social development until at least 8-10 weeks (puppies) or 10-12 weeks (kittens). Rabbit kits follow a different rhythm: alfalfa-based diet only, greens delayed until well after weaning. This tool builds a species-specific week-by-week plan from the litter''s birth date.',
    'Weaning Schedule (Puppies, Kittens, Rabbits) — Free Pet Tool',
    'Weaning is a gradual process, not a switch. Puppies and kittens should be introduced to solid food around week 3-4, transitioned over 3-5 weeks, and fully weaned by week 7-8 — but they should stay with mom and littermates for social development until at least 8-10 weeks (puppies) or 10-12 weeks (kittens). Rabbit kits follow a different rhythm: alfalfa-based diet only, greens delayed until well after weaning. This tool builds a species-specific week-by-week plan from the litter''s birth date.', 0, 0, 193
  );
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tool_overrides (slug, title_override, description_override, seo_title, seo_description, featured, disabled, sort_order) VALUES (
    'newborn-care-timeline', 'Newborn Care Timeline', 'The first 12 weeks of a puppy or kitten''s life have more milestones than any other period. Colostrum in the first 2 hours, eyes opening around day 10-14, first solid food at 3-4 weeks, first vaccines at 6-8 weeks, socialization windows that close forever if missed. This timeline lays out every stage from day 0 to rehoming, with the tasks a breeder or foster caregiver needs to complete at each step. Follow it closely — the difference between a well-adjusted puppy or kitten and a problem adult is set in these weeks.',
    'Newborn Care Timeline — Free Pet Tool',
    'The first 12 weeks of a puppy or kitten''s life have more milestones than any other period. Colostrum in the first 2 hours, eyes opening around day 10-14, first solid food at 3-4 weeks, first vaccines at 6-8 weeks, socialization windows that close forever if missed. This timeline lays out every stage from day 0 to rehoming, with the tasks a breeder or foster caregiver needs to complete at each step. Follow it closely — the difference between a well-adjusted puppy or kitten and a problem adult is set in these weeks.', 1, 0, 194
  );
